+            /// D175a -- bounded early planting: break the "chopping always wins" priority
+            /// (B4.4/B4.5). `main_candidates`'s own first branch converts a carried seed
+            /// straight to a bank trip (toward wood) whenever `safe_regeneration` is set
+            /// (true in production), and otherwise a unit only ever considers PLANT via
+            /// `endgame_candidates`, reached only once it has nothing left to CHOP
+            /// (median turn 191.5 in the field vs 21-29 for two-worker peers). This adds
+            /// a competing, scored candidate -- not a rewrite of that existing logic --
+            /// so it wins by priority (score) rather than by starving CHOP of targets.
+            ///
+            /// Frozen five-condition conjunction (D175a protocol, exact, no scope beyond
+            /// this), re-evaluated fresh every call, no cross-turn state of its own:
+            /// (a) the worker carries a plantable seed, or can PICK one from an adjacent
+            ///     own-bank source this turn (the exact adjacency + non-empty-bank-stock
+            ///     gate `main_candidates`/`endgame_candidates` already use elsewhere for
+            ///     PICK -- no new routing);
+            /// (b) our live own-crop count is < 6 (`own_crops`, tracked read-only in
+            ///     `reconcile_opponent_crops`; peers' measured concurrent ceiling ~5-6);
+            /// (c) turn <= 120 (early-economy window; roster already reaches 2 by median
+            ///     turn 7, so timing is not the binding constraint, priority is);
+            /// (d) a legal (unoccupied-by-a-plant, unoccupied-by-another-own-unit) cell
+            ///     exists within BFS distance <= 2 of the worker's current position --
+            ///     no detours (the D174a lesson);
+            /// (e) not bill-critical (no existing `tree_commitments` entry for this unit
+            ///     -- the file's one existing "this chop is protected" signal, itself
+            ///     inert whenever `tree_target_bonus <= 0`, true in production) and not
+            ///     `Self::endgame(view)` (turn>250 OR board-stripped-and-losing, reused
+            ///     verbatim, not re-derived).
+            ///
+            /// Scored to outrank ordinary CHOP (`1000 * wood/turns`, rarely > a few
+            /// thousand) and this file's own `bank_candidates` (max 8,000) while staying
+            /// below the unconditional-override tier (`forced_move` 20,000; the inert
+            /// scarce-farming path 11,000-12,000) -- same "governance tier" convention
+            /// `endgame_candidates`'s own PLANT-at-target (9,000) already uses.
+            fn bounded_early_plant_candidate(
